You may convey a covered work under sections 3 and 4 of this License
without being bound by section 3 of the GNU GPL.

2. Conveying Modified Versions.

If you modify a copy of the Library, and, in your modifications,
a facility refers to a function or data to be supplied by an
Application that uses the facility (other than as an argument passed
when the facility is invoked), then you may convey a copy of the
modified version:

a) under this License, provided that you make a good faith effort to
ensure that, in the event an Application does not supply the
function or data, the facility still operates, and performs
whatever part of its purpose remains meaningful, or

b) under the GNU GPL, with none of the additional permissions of
this License applicable to that copy.

3. Object Code Incorporating Material from Library Header Files.

The object code form of an Application may incorporate material from
a header file that is part of the Library. You may convey such object
code under terms of your choice, provided that, if the incorporated
material is not limited to numerical parameters, data structure
layouts and accessors, or small macros, inline functions and templates
(ten or fewer instructions in length), you do both of the following:

a) Give prominent notice with each copy of the object code that the
Library is used in it and that the Library and its use are covered by
this License.

b) Accompany the object code with a copy of this License.

4. Combined Works.

You may convey a Combined Work under terms of your choice that,
taken together, effectively do not restrict modification of the
portions of the Library contained in the Combined Work and do not
restrict reverse engineering, debugging, or other analysis of
the Combined Work, provided that you also do each of the following:

a) Give prominent notice with each copy of the Combined Work that
the Library is used in it and that the Library and its use are
covered by this License.

b) Accompany the Combined Work with a copy of this License.

c) For a Combined Work that displays copyright notices during
execution, include the copyright notice for the Library among
these notices, as well as a reference directing the user to the
copies of this License and the GNU GPL included with the Combined Work.

d) Do one of the following:

0) Convey the Minimal Corresponding Source under the terms of this
License, and the Corresponding Application Code in a form suitable
for, and under terms that allow, the user to recombine or
relocate the Application with a modified version of the Library to
produce a modified Combined Work, developed by the user, in a way
that the Modified Library is implemented using the same interface
as the original version of the Library. The Modified Library may
be the original version of the Library or any version of the
Library with which the Combined Work was made, or any other
version of the Library that the user can obtain by recombining
or relocating the Application with a different version of the
Library.

1) Use a suitable shared library mechanism for linking with the
Library. A suitable mechanism is one that (a) uses at runtime a
copy of the Library already present on the user's computer system
and (b) will operate properly with a modified version of the
Library that is interface-compatible with the version of the
Library with which the Combined Work was made.

e) Provide Installation Information, but only if you would otherwise
be required to provide such information under section 6 of the
GNU GPL, and only to the extent that such information is necessary
for the user to install and execute a modified version of the
Combined Work produced by modifying the Library. If the Library
and the Combined Work are a single object file or program, and
the Application is part of the Combined Work, you need only provide
Installation Information for the Application.

5. Combined Libraries.

You may place library facilities that are a covered work side by side
in a single library together with other library facilities that are
not covered by this License, and convey such a combined library under
terms of your choice, if you do both of the following:

a) Accompany the combined library with a copy of this License.

b) Give prominent notice with the combined library that part of it
is covered by this License, and explain how to find the Library
facilities that are covered by this License.

